senses.gloss:
(VI)--the milk-white humped bull born of सुरभी and the standard of शिव;
1: Br. III. 3. ७८-79; ७४. ४८-51; IV. १४. 2.
taught Godharma to दीर्घतमस्;
2: Ib. III. ७४. ४७;
gift of, in a श्राद्ध.
3: Ib. III. १९. १५.

--शिव with the standard of the bull; also वृषवाहन;
1: M. 1. 8; १३३. १३; वा. ३०. १८०, २६१; Vi. V. ३३. ५०; ३४. ३५.
prayed to by काम and others;
2: M. १४०. ८५; १९१. ११५; १९२. २७; २०६. २७ and २८.
see वृषध्वज the Lord of Rudras.
3: वा. ७०. 6.

--rule with गुरुण्डस् (मरुण्डस्-वा। प्।); both Mlecchas;
1: Br. III. ७४. १७७; वा. ५८. ८८; ९९. ३६३.
joined with the Mlecchas;
2: M. २७३. २२.
to be put down by future Kalki.
3: Ib. ४७. २५२; वा. ९८. ११४.

(II)--a son of सात्वत and father of Sumitra and युजाजित्;
1: भा. IX. २४. 6 and १२.
darling of the Yadus; had two wives, गान्धारी and माद्री; the former bore Sumitra and the latter, five children;
2: M. ४४. ४८; ४५. 1-2.
suspected कृष्ण of having appropriated the syamantaka gem from which he honourably redeemed himself;
3: Br. III. ७१. 1, ३६, १०२.
belonged to the कृओष्ठु line;
4: Ib. III. ७०. १५; ७३. ९१.
originator of the वृष्णि kula.
5: वा. ९५. १४.

--the community of द्वारवती in which Bala- राम and कृष्ण were born;
1: भा. I. 3. २३; ११. ११; १४. २५; Br. III. ६१. २३; ७१. ८५; वा. 1. १४५; ९६. ८४, १७५; ८६. २८.
कुन्ती was attached to these people while Kamsa devised means to vanquish them. Were relieved at Kamsa's death.
2: भा. I. 8. ४१; X. ३६. ३३; ३९. २५; ४५. १५;
Its name derived from वृष्णि.
3: Ib. IX. २३. ३०.
They praised the heroic deeds of कृष्ण who was their Lord and who lived with them. But they did not recognise in Him the Almighty Lord;
4: Ib. I. 9. १८; II. 4. २०; IX. २४. ६३; X. 1. ११ and ६२; ९०. ४६.
ended their lives by fighting their kinsmen at प्रभासा. Attained Hari through relationship.
5: Ib. XI. ३०. १८; VII. 1. ३०.
